IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc21-part-17.l4 -- PART XVII, Language of Accused, ss 530 to 534 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Written from the text alone; takes nobody's point of view. Imports the keel's core only.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements. A result is a MAYBE BOOLEAN where the text can leave a case unanswered:
--   JUST TRUE  the case is within the rule, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words (a failed "if", "where", "on application", a period the text fixes, a flat exclusion): every such
--              branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"`;
--   NOTHING    not covered: every such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. The marginal readings are listed in NOTES.md.
-- `-- GRANT-GATE: if` marks a power whose "if" gate failing answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); `-- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period` marks a power
-- whose gate is "where", "when", "upon", "on application" or a stated period, left as the guide's rulings give it (JUST FALSE) for a lawyer; `-- CLAIM-NAMED` marks a
-- function named for a right the person holds ("have the right", "entitled"), also left for a lawyer. NOTES.md counts each group.

§ `PART XVII -- Language of Accused`

§§ `Section 530 -- Language of accused`

-- 530 (1) On application by an accused whose language is one of the official languages of Canada, made not later than the time of the appearance at which the trial date is set,
-- a judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace shall grant an order that the accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks
-- the official language of the accused or, if the circumstances warrant, both official languages. A duty. The time is taken as a calendar date (NOTES.md fork F1).
-- src:11831 | 530 (1) On application by an accused whose language is one of the official languages of Canada, made not later than the time of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set, a judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace shall grant an order directing that the accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury, as the case may be, who speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or, if the circumstances warrant, who speak both official languages of Canada.
@ref s 530(1) (src:11831-11831)
GIVEN `the accused's language is one of the official languages of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has applied for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the accused applied` IS A DATE
      `the date of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(1) the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall grant the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused's language is one of the official languages of Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused whose language is one of the official languages of Canada"
        IF NOT `the accused has applied for an order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by an accused"
        IF NOT (`the date on which the accused applied` AT MOST `the date of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made not later than the time of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 530(1), the content of the order: the language of the accused, or both official languages "if the circumstances warrant".
-- src:11831 | 530 (1) On application by an accused whose language is one of the official languages of Canada, made not later than the time of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set, a judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace shall grant an order directing that the accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury, as the case may be, who speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or, if the circumstances warrant, who speak both official languages of Canada.
@ref s 530(1) (src:11831-11831)
GIVEN `the court shall grant the order under subsection 530(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances warrant trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(1) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court shall grant the order under subsection 530(1)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the order is granted is for s 530(1), and that is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no order is granted under subsection (1), so the text gives it no content
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the circumstances warrant trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the circumstances warrant"

-- 530 (2) The same, for an accused whose language is not one of the official languages: the order MAY be granted, for the official language in which the accused, in the opinion of
-- the court, can best give testimony or, if the circumstances warrant, both. A power; the gate is "on application" and a stated time.
-- src:11833 | (2) On application by an accused whose language is not one of the official languages of Canada, made not later than the time of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set, a judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace may grant an order directing that the accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury, as the case may be, who speak the official language of Canada in which the accused, in the opinion of the judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace, can best give testimony or, if the circumstances warrant, who speak both official languages of Canada.
@ref s 530(2) (src:11833-11833)
GIVEN `the accused's language is one of the official languages of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has applied for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the accused applied` IS A DATE
      `the date of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(2) the judge, provincial court judge or justice may grant the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the accused's language is one of the official languages of Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused whose language is not one of the official languages of Canada"
        IF NOT `the accused has applied for an order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by an accused"
        IF NOT (`the date on which the accused applied` AT MOST `the date of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made not later than the time of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11833 | (2) On application by an accused whose language is not one of the official languages of Canada, made not later than the time of the appearance of the accused at which their trial date is set, a judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace may grant an order directing that the accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury, as the case may be, who speak the official language of Canada in which the accused, in the opinion of the judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace, can best give testimony or, if the circumstances warrant, who speak both official languages of Canada.
@ref s 530(2) (src:11833-11833)
GIVEN `the court may grant the order under subsection 530(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances warrant trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(2) the order directs trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court may grant the order under subsection 530(2)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order may be granted is for s 530(2), and that is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no order may be granted under subsection (2), so the text gives it no content
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the circumstances warrant trial before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the circumstances warrant"

-- 530 (3) The judge or justice before whom an accused first appears shall ensure that they are advised of their right to apply for an order and of the time before which the application must be made.
-- src:11835 | (3) The judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace before whom an accused first appears shall ensure that they are advised of their right to apply for an order under subsection (1) or (2) and of the time before which such an application must be made.
@ref s 530(3) (src:11835-11835)
GIVEN `the accused first appears before this judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(3) the judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace shall ensure that the accused is advised of the right and of the time` MEANS
    IF `the accused first appears before this judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before whom an accused first appears"

-- 530 (4) If the accused fails to apply, and the court is satisfied that it is in the best interests of justice that the accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks the language,
-- the court may, if it does not speak that language, by order remand the accused to be tried by one who does. A power; every gate is an "if".
-- src:11837 | (4) If an accused fails to apply for an order under subsection (1) or (2) and the judge, provincial court judge, judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice or justice of the peace before whom the accused is to be tried, in this Part referred to as “the court”, is satisfied that it is in the best interests of justice that the accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury who speak the official language of Canada that is the language of the accused or, if the language of the accused is not one of the official languages of Canada, the official language of Canada in which the accused, in the opinion of the court, can best give testimony, the court may, if it does not speak that language, by order remand the accused to be tried by a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury, as the case may be, who speak that language or, if the circumstances warrant, who speak both official languages of Canada.
@ref s 530(4) (src:11837-11837)
GIVEN `the accused has failed to apply for an order under subsection 530(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is in the best interests of justice that the accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court speaks that language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(4) the court may by order remand the accused to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused has failed to apply for an order under subsection 530(1) or (2)` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an accused fails to apply for an order under subsection (1) or (2)"
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that it is in the best interests of justice that the accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks that language` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is satisfied that it is in the best interests of justice"
        IF `the court speaks that language` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it does not speak that language"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 530 (5) An order under this section that a trial be held in one of the official languages may, if the circumstances warrant, be varied by the court to require both, and vice versa.
-- src:11839 | (5) An order under this section that a trial be held in one of the official languages of Canada may, if the circumstances warrant, be varied by the court to require that it be held in both official languages of Canada, and vice versa.
@ref s 530(5) (src:11839-11839)
DECLARE `s 530(5) what the order under section 530 requires` IS ONE OF
    `s 530(5) one official language of Canada`
    `s 530(5) both official languages of Canada`
    `s 530(5) there is no order under section 530`

-- src:11839 | (5) An order under this section that a trial be held in one of the official languages of Canada may, if the circumstances warrant, be varied by the court to require that it be held in both official languages of Canada, and vice versa.
@ref s 530(5) (src:11839-11839)
GIVEN `the order as made` IS A `s 530(5) what the order under section 530 requires`
      `the circumstances warrant the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(5) the court may vary the order to require the other` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order as made` EQUALS `s 530(5) there is no order under section 530` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order under this section"
        IF NOT `the circumstances warrant the variation` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the circumstances warrant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 530 (6) The facts that two or more accused who are to be tried together are each entitled to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks one of the official languages, and that those languages are different,
-- may constitute circumstances that warrant an order for both. "May constitute": a sufficient circumstance, not the only one.
-- src:11841 | (6) The facts that two or more accused who are to be tried together are each entitled to be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury who speak one of the official languages of Canada and that those official languages are different may constitute circumstances that warrant that an order be granted directing that they be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury who speak both official languages of Canada.
@ref s 530(6) (src:11841-11841)
GIVEN `two or more accused are to be tried together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each is entitled to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks one of the official languages of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those official languages are different` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(6) the facts may constitute circumstances that warrant an order for both official languages` MEANS
    IF `two or more accused are to be tried together` AND `each is entitled to be tried before a justice or judge who speaks one of the official languages of Canada` AND `those official languages are different`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may constitute circumstances that warrant"

§§ `Section 530.01 -- Translation of documents`

-- 530.01 (1) If an order is granted under section 530, a prosecutor, other than a private prosecutor, shall, on application by the accused, (a) cause the portions of an information or indictment that are in
-- an official language that is not that of the accused (or that in which the accused can best give testimony) to be translated into the other official language.
-- src:11843 | 530.01 (1) If an order is granted under section 530, a prosecutor — other than a private prosecutor — shall, on application by the accused,
-- src:11844 | (a) cause the portions of an information or indictment against the accused that are in an official language that is not that of the accused or that in which the accused can best give testimony to be translated into the other official language; and
@ref s 530.01(1)(a) (src:11843-11844)
GIVEN `an order is granted under section 530` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor is a private prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has applied for the translation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a portion of the information or indictment is in an official language that is not that of the accused or that in which the accused can best give testimony` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.01(1)(a) the prosecutor shall cause the portions to be translated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is granted under section 530` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is granted under section 530"
        IF `the prosecutor is a private prosecutor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a private prosecutor"
        IF NOT `the accused has applied for the translation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the accused"
        IF NOT `a portion of the information or indictment is in an official language that is not that of the accused or that in which the accused can best give testimony` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the portions of an information or indictment against the accused that are in an official language that is not that of the accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 530.01 (1)(b) ... and (b) provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time. Same gates as (a): the copy is of the translation (a) requires.
-- src:11845 | (b) provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time.
@ref s 530.01(1)(b) (src:11845-11845)
GIVEN `the answer of s 530.01(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.01(1)(b) the prosecutor shall provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 530.01(1)(a)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) provides a copy "of the translated text", and whether there is a translated text is for paragraph (a), which is not settled
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is granted under section 530"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE

-- 530.01 (2) In the case of a discrepancy between the original version of a document and the translated text, the original version shall prevail.
-- src:11847 | (2) In the case of a discrepancy between the original version of a document and the translated text, the original version shall prevail.
@ref s 530.01(2) (src:11847-11847)
GIVEN `there is a discrepancy between the original version of a document and the translated text` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.01(2) the original version prevails` MEANS
    IF `there is a discrepancy between the original version of a document and the translated text`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a discrepancy"

§§ `Section 530.1 -- If order granted`

-- 530.1 If an order is granted under section 530: (a) the accused and his counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes during the preliminary inquiry and trial of the accused.
-- src:11849 | 530.1 If an order is granted under section 530,
-- src:11850 | (a) the accused and his counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes during the preliminary inquiry and trial of the accused;
@ref s 530.1(a) (src:11849-11850)
GIVEN `an order is granted under section 530` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stage of the proceedings` IS A `Stage of the proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.1(a) the accused and counsel have the right to use either official language for all purposes` MEANS   -- CLAIM-NAMED
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is granted under section 530` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is granted under section 530"
        IF NOT (`the stage of the proceedings` EQUALS `preliminary inquiry` OR `the stage of the proceedings` EQUALS `trial`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "during the preliminary inquiry and trial of the accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (b) the accused and his counsel may use either official language in written pleadings or other documents used in any proceedings relating to the preliminary inquiry or trial of the accused.
-- src:11851 | (b) the accused and his counsel may use either official language in written pleadings or other documents used in any proceedings relating to the preliminary inquiry or trial of the accused;
@ref s 530.1(b) (src:11851-11851)
GIVEN `an order is granted under section 530` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.1(b) the accused and counsel may use either official language in written pleadings or other documents` MEANS
    IF `an order is granted under section 530`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an order is granted under section 530"

