`s 530.1(h) the court shall make the written trial judgment available in the official language of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is granted under section 530` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an order is granted under section 530"
        IF NOT `the trial judgment is issued in writing in either official language` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "issued in writing in either official language"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 530.2 -- Language used in proceeding`

-- 530.2 (1) If an order is granted directing that an accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages, the justice or judge presiding over a preliminary inquiry or trial
-- may, at the start of the proceeding, make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, the prosecutor and the justice or judge may use each official language.
-- src:11863 | 530.2 (1) If an order is granted directing that an accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury who speak both official languages, the justice or judge presiding over a preliminary inquiry or trial may, at the start of the proceeding, make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, the prosecutor and the justice or judge may use each official language.
@ref s 530.2(1) (src:11863-11863)
GIVEN `an order is granted directing that the accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stage of the proceedings` IS A `Stage of the proceedings`
      `the order is made at the start of the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.2(1) the justice or judge presiding may make an order setting out the circumstances in which, and the extent to which, each official language may be used` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is granted directing that the accused be tried before a justice or judge who speaks both official languages` THEN NOTHING   -- GRANT-GATE: if -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an order is granted directing that an accused be tried before a justice of the peace, provincial court judge, judge or judge and jury who speak both official languages"
        IF NOT (`the stage of the proceedings` EQUALS `preliminary inquiry` OR `the stage of the proceedings` EQUALS `trial`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "presiding over a preliminary inquiry or trial"
        IF NOT `the order is made at the start of the proceeding` THEN JUST FALSE   -- GRANT-GATE: where/when/upon/period -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the start of the proceeding"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 530.2 (2) Any order granted under this section shall, to the extent possible, respect the right of the accused to be tried in his or her official language.
-- src:11865 | (2) Any order granted under this section shall, to the extent possible, respect the right of the accused to be tried in his or her official language.
@ref s 530.2(2) (src:11865-11865)
GIVEN `an order is granted under section 530.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530.2(2) the order shall, to the extent possible, respect the right of the accused to be tried in their official language` MEANS
    IF `an order is granted under section 530.2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any order granted under this section"

§§ `Section 531 -- Change of venue`

-- 531 Despite any other provision of this Act but subject to any regulations made under section 533, if an order made under section 530 cannot be conveniently complied with in the territorial division
-- in which the offence would otherwise be tried, the court shall, except if that territorial division is in the Province of New Brunswick, order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province.
-- src:11867 | 531 Despite any other provision of this Act but subject to any regulations made under section 533, if an order made under section 530 cannot be conveniently complied with in the territorial division in which the offence would otherwise be tried, the court shall, except if that territorial division is in the Province of New Brunswick, order that the trial of the accused be held in another territorial division in the same province.
@ref s 531 (src:11867-11867)
GIVEN `an order was made under section 530` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order cannot be conveniently complied with in the territorial division in which the offence would otherwise be tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province or territory in which that territorial division lies` IS A `Province or territory`
      `a regulation made under section 533 governs the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 531 the court shall order that the trial be held in another territorial division in the same province` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a regulation made under section 533 governs the case` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any regulations made under section 533"
        IF NOT `an order was made under section 530` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an order made under section 530"
        IF NOT `the order cannot be conveniently complied with in the territorial division in which the offence would otherwise be tried` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cannot be conveniently complied with in the territorial division"
        IF `the province or territory in which that territorial division lies` EQUALS `New Brunswick` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except if that territorial division is in the Province of New Brunswick"
        IF `the province or territory in which that territorial division lies` EQUALS Yukon OR `the province or territory in which that territorial division lies` EQUALS `Northwest Territories` OR `the province or territory in which that territorial division lies` EQUALS Nunavut THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the section speaks of "the same province" and the sources do not say whether a territory is a province
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 532 -- Saving`

-- 532 Nothing in this Part or the Official Languages Act derogates from or otherwise adversely affects any right afforded by a law of a province in force on the coming into force of this Part in that province
-- or thereafter coming into force relating to the language of proceedings or testimony in criminal matters that is not inconsistent with this Part or that Act.
-- src:11869 | 532 Nothing in this Part or the Official Languages Act derogates from or otherwise adversely affects any right afforded by a law of a province in force on the coming into force of this Part in that province or thereafter coming into force relating to the language of proceedings or testimony in criminal matters that is not inconsistent with this Part or that Act.
@ref s 532 (src:11869-11869)
GIVEN `the right is afforded by a law of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law was in force on the coming into force of this Part in that province or comes into force after it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right relates to the language of proceedings or testimony in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is inconsistent with this Part or the Official Languages Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 532 this Part and the Official Languages Act do not derogate from the right` MEANS
    IF `the right is afforded by a law of a province` AND `the law was in force on the coming into force of this Part in that province or comes into force after it` AND `the right relates to the language of proceedings or testimony in criminal matters` AND NOT `the right is inconsistent with this Part or the Official Languages Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is not inconsistent with this Part or that Act"

§§ `Section 533 -- Regulations; section 533.1 -- Review; section 534 -- Repealed`

-- 533 (regulations) and 533.1 (review by a parliamentary committee) are machinery: no rule is encoded (NOTES.md coverage, reason 2). 534 is shown repealed; the text shows:
-- src:11876 | 534 [Repealed, 1997, c. 18, s. 63]
@ref s 534 (src:11876-11876)
`s 534 repealed` MEANS "534 [Repealed, 1997, c. 18, s. 63]"

§§ `Section 530.01(1) as a duty in time: the prosecutor's two steps (regulative rule)`

-- src:11843 | 530.01 (1) If an order is granted under section 530, a prosecutor — other than a private prosecutor — shall, on application by the accused,
-- src:11844 | (a) cause the portions of an information or indictment against the accused that are in an official language that is not that of the accused or that in which the accused can best give testimony to be translated into the other official language; and
-- src:11845 | (b) provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time.
@ref s 530.01(1) (src:11843-11845)
DECLARE `s 530.01(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 530.01(1) causes the portions to be translated`
    `s 530.01(1) provides the accused with a written copy of the translated text`

-- The text names the party (a prosecutor, other than a private prosecutor), the two steps in order, and no number of days ("at the earliest possible time"), so there is no WITHIN and no LEST:
-- nothing is invented. A trace shows the two steps in sequence.
-- src:11843 | 530.01 (1) If an order is granted under section 530, a prosecutor — other than a private prosecutor — shall, on application by the accused,
-- src:11844 | (a) cause the portions of an information or indictment against the accused that are in an official language that is not that of the accused or that in which the accused can best give testimony to be translated into the other official language; and
-- src:11845 | (b) provide the accused with a written copy of the translated text at the earliest possible time.
@ref s 530.01(1) (src:11843-11845)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 530.01(1) action`
`s 530.01(1) the prosecutor must have the portions translated and then give the accused a written copy` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 530.01(1) causes the portions to be translated`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the prosecutor`
        MUST `s 530.01(1) provides the accused with a written copy of the translated text`
        HENCE FULFILLED
